-Owner skill: `skill://ipc-contract`. Thin Tauri shell over `yamt_session::MergeSession` and `yamt_lsp_host::Host`, or with `--diff` over `yamt_compare::TabStore` (plan §2 #93–#97, #101), or with `--diff=<range>` over `yamt_range::Range` and the pair's review threads in `yamt_review::ThreadStore` (plan §2 #103–#107, #117–#119), with `--ai` also over the AI's `yamt_agent::Workspace` (plan §2 #108–#111, #114): `lib.rs` (`run`, `export_bindings`) shared by both bins; `graphics.rs` (NVIDIA guard: the first statement of `run()`, the project's one `unsafe` line, plan §2 #43), `args.rs` (`yamt [--repo <path>]` → `Merge`, `yamt --diff` → `Compare`, `yamt --diff=<a>..<b>`/`--diff=<a>...<b>` with `--repo <path>` in either order → `Range { spec, repo, ai }` through `RangeSpec::parse`, whose error is the usage line; `--diff` with `--repo` is a usage error, so is `--diff` with a `--diff=` or a second `--diff=` ("give --diff or one --diff=<range>, not both"); `--help`/`--version` win; `--ai` is accepted with every mode and never stored, only `Range` keeps it as `Ai` = `Off` | `On`, plan §2 #108), `appimage.rs` (inside an AppImage — `APPIMAGE` and `APPDIR` set and the binary under `$APPDIR` — a relative `--repo` is resolved against `OWD`; never chdir, WebKit's helper paths are relative to `$APPDIR/usr`; called for `Merge` and `Range`, never for `Compare`), `outcome.rs` (start-up decision, exit status 0/1/2; the close ending, `ending_when_git_is_done` — `ending_on_close` once `lock_when_git_is_done` lets go: `Finished(kind)` 0 with `<operation> finished`, `Aborted(kind)` 1 with `<operation> aborted` (`merge aborted` for a merge), reading and writing nothing; `Held` lists through `refresh_stop` and counts git's view, a `MovedOn` there counting the stop git moved on to like `MovedOn`; `MovedOn` opens the stop git is at only to count its unmerged files, settling nothing), `merge.rs` (`Merge` = `Held(Box<MergeSession>)` | `Running(kind)` | `MovedOn { root, highest_disk_version }` | `Aborted(kind)` | `Finished(kind)`, the app's merge state as `MergeState` = `Mutex<Merge>`; `session()` answers `GitRunning`, `StopMovedOn`, `MergeAborted` or `MergeFinished` outside `Held` — the one state → refusal mapping, also what a worker hand-over refuses with; `has_ended()` is true only for `Finished`/`Aborted`; `list_stop` opens the new stop after a move with `MergeSession::open_after(root, highest_disk_version)`, so its disk versions start above the old session's and a write meant for the old stop is refused (#1383), becomes `MovedOn` when git moved on, and builds `Listing::Files` from session's `StopList` by an exhaustive destructure, so a new field does not compile until it is listed; every `MovedOn` is built by `moved_on(&session)` (root and `highest_disk_version()`); `abort_operation`/`continue_operation` hand the session to a `spawn_blocking` worker while `Running` and put the outcome back: refused → `Held`, the stop moved on outside yamt (`StopMovedOn`) → `MovedOn`, so the next `list_stop` opens git's stop (#1440), stopped → `MovedOn`, a panicked worker → `MovedOn` built before the hand-over, answering `StopMovedOn` like every later call (the window goes to the next stop) and logging the join error with `tracing::error!`; `lock_when_git_is_done` makes the close ending wait for git; plan §2 #74, #88, #89; its tests in `merge/tests.rs`), `compare.rs` (the compare window, plan §2 #94/#95/#97: `manage_store_in` opens `TabStore` and manages it as `CompareState` in `<data_dir>/yamt/compare/` before any window, its failure the one line `yamt --diff` ends with (exit 2); `CompareState` = `Mutex<TabStore>`; the eight commands `open_compare`, `load_tab`, `set_column`, `add_tab`, `close_tab`, `rename_tab`, `set_tab_language`, `show_tab`; `load_tab`/`set_column` run on a `spawn_blocking` worker that locks the store only to call it, then builds the reply (`tab_texts`/`comparison`, the diff) after the lock is released; a worker that panicked answers `WorkerStopped`), `range.rs` (the range window, plan §2 #103–#107, #117: `run_range` resolves the range before any app is built — not a repository, an unknown name, no merge base: one `yamt: …` line, exit 2, no window —, builds the app with `with_commands`, takes the pair's `PairLock` under `<data_dir>/yamt/range/` before listing (another window on the same pair: one line naming both short ids, exit 2), then opens the pair folder's `threads.json` with `ThreadStore::open` before any window (unreadable, broken or newer: one `yamt: …` line naming the file, exit 2, the file untouched) and logs the stored paths the range does not list once with `tracing::warn!`; manages the AI's state through `ai::manage` and `RangeState { range, threads: Mutex<ThreadStore>, sending: Mutex<()>, _lock }` (the range itself never changes after start), opens the window titled `<range as typed> — <repository folder> — yamt` and, once it closed, runs `ai::end_at_exit`, then ends with exit 0 and no message; never a `MergeSession`, `HostState` or `TabStore`; the two commands `open_range` (`Range::start`) and `load_range_file` (`Range::load` on a `spawn_blocking` worker, a panic → `WorkerStopped`); its test helpers `open_range_window`/`open_range_window_with(ai)`/`open_range_window_in(repo, data, ai)`/`open_range_window_on(repo, range)` (Unix only)/`RangeWindow` are shared with `review.rs` and `ai.rs`), `ai.rs` (the range window's AI, plan §2 #108–#111, #114: `AiState` = `Off` | `On(Workspace)`, managed as `Mutex<AiState>` by every range window; `AiState::workspace()` is the one `AiOff` mapping, the private `lock` the only way to the state; `manage` builds the `Workspace` (repository root, pair folder, the right commit's full id) only in its `Ai::On` arm and there starts a background thread that holds the state while `Workspace::remove_own_leftovers` removes this pair's partial and removing folders, `manage` returning once it holds it, so no checkout of the pair is made or removed meanwhile; the thread then releases the state and runs `yamt_agent::sweep_other_pairs` without it, so the looks at every other pair's kept checkout never hold up a command; `stop_agent_on_page_start(app, event)`: a page that starts loading stops the agent with `try_lock`; while a prepare, a start, a discard or the own-pair sweep holds the state, a thread waits for the lock and stops the agent then (deferred, never dropped), the checkout kept; `end_at_exit` takes the workspace out and calls `Workspace::end` (stop and reap the agent, look again, remove only a clean checkout); the seven commands `prepare_checkout` (on a `spawn_blocking` worker, under the lock), `start_agent` (a worker command: under the lock it stops and reaps an earlier agent — up to about 3 s — and spawns the new one; a small thread forwards the agent's events into its `Channel` through `servers::forward`), `send_to_agent`, `stop_agent`, `checkout_changes` (the `LookJob` taken under the lock, git's look on the worker after it is released), `discard_checkout` (worker, under the lock while the folder is removed; a failed removal → `RemoveFailed`), `diff_texts` (worker, `yamt_compare::text_differences`, needs no AI state, a side over 8 MiB → `ColumnTooLarge`)), `review.rs` (the range window's threads and posting, plan §2 #117–#119, #121: `list_threads`, `add_thread`, `add_note`, `queue_message`, `unqueue_message`, `set_thread_session`, `add_ai_answer` lock `threads`, call one `ThreadStore` method with the range and let go; `check_gitlab` and `send_queue` run on a `spawn_blocking` worker (a panic → `WorkerStopped`) with the glab `yamt_review::Glab::find()` finds on PATH at each call; `send_queue` takes the send guard with `try_lock` — another send running answers `SendRunning`, a guard poisoned by a panicked send is taken again — and holds it for the whole send, while `yamt_review::send_queue` locks `threads` only between glab calls; each `SendProgress` goes to the call's `Channel`, a failed send logged; its Unix-only `through_glab` tests run `send_queue` and `check_gitlab` in a child test process whose PATH starts with the committed `scripts/fake-glab`, on `scripts/range-repo.sh`'s `main...feature` and the scenarios `tests/glab/slow-post` and `lined-up`), `clipboard.rs` (`read_clipboard(selection: ClipboardSelection)` → the text or `None`, for every window, no managed state, plan §2 #99: on Linux GTK's text request (`gtk::Clipboard::request_text`), started on the main thread by `run_on_main_thread` and waited for on a `spawn_blocking` worker, so a hung owner never blocks the window; it never asks GTK for the selection's format list — no `request_targets`, `wait_for_targets`, `wait_is_*_available`, `wait_for_contents`, `request_contents` — since WebKitGTK 2.54 crashes on a failed one; other systems answer `None`), `window.rs` (one window per run, merge, compare or range, built by one `open_and_wait` (`pub(crate)` with `context()` and `window_title`, for `range.rs`): reads `stored_at_start` once — theme and antialiasing — and applies font rendering before building the webview with the start script; `WindowKind` (`name()`: merge, compare or range); `open_with_data_folder(title, kind, ai, manage, at_exit)`: `manage` before the window, `at_exit` after it closed; close fallback: a close request between `UNANSWERED_CLOSE_GRACE` and `UNANSWERED_CLOSE_TIMEOUT` after an unanswered one destroys the window; after the event loop the merge window runs `stop_all` so no language server outlives a normal close, then the ending once git is done; the compare window, titled `Compare — yamt`, never opens a `MergeSession`, runs git or manages `Mutex<Merge>`/`HostState`, and ends with exit 0 and no message), `start_script.rs` (`start_script(theme, kind, ai)`: sets `<html data-theme>` and `<html data-window="merge|compare|range">` before the first frame, and `<html data-ai="on">` only for a range window started with `--ai`), `font_rendering.rs` (Linux: the Antialiasing setting onto GTK's `gtk-xft-antialias`/`gtk-xft-rgba` before the webview is built, plan §2 #60), `commands.rs` (commands ≤ 15 lines delegating to `session` through `Merge::session`, or to `merge.rs`; the two async commands destroy the window only when `Merge::has_ended()` (finished or aborted, never after `Stopped`), which ends the event loop without a close request, so the page asks nothing; they take the window and read the state from it, since tauri's check of an async command with a borrowed argument expands to an `unreachable!`; `specta_builder` registers every command of every window; `with_session` manages `Mutex<Merge>`, calls `servers::manage` for the host, sets the invoke handler and registers the merge window's page-load hook: a page that starts loading calls `servers::stop_runs_on_page_start`; `with_commands` (the compare and range windows) sets the invoke handler and its page-load hook: a page that starts loading calls `ai::stop_agent_on_page_start` with the app handle, which does nothing without a `Mutex<AiState>` (every range window manages one, never the compare window); Tauri keeps only the last `on_page_load`, so each builder registers one), `servers.rs` (`manage`: builds and manages the `HostState` (`Mutex<Host>`) for the session's repository, nothing else; `stop_runs_on_page_start`: on `PageLoadEvent::Started` stops every run of the page before it (`Host::stop_every`), since a reloaded page's channels still take events; `forward`: the one rule that hands a run's events to its Tauri `Channel` and, when a send fails, drops them so the run stops itself, used by `start_server` and `ai::start_agent`; the six language server commands, plan §2 #70: `servers_context`, `start_server`, `send_to_server`, `stop_server`, `find_program`, `project_files`; its Unix-only test helpers `channel_into` and `is_alive` are shared with `ai.rs`), `settings.rs` (`Places` and the eight settings commands; `set_server_answer` and `set_server_switch` (a found server switched off or on, plan §2 #83) key their change by the host's root, and a root that is not UTF-8 only reads), `ipc_error.rs` (`IpcError`, mapped from `yamt_session::Error` — git's refusal of a Continue is `Git` with git's own text —, from `yamt_settings::Error`, from `yamt_compare::Error` (a stored-tabs problem is `ReadFailed`, `UnknownTab`, a column over the limit `ColumnTooLarge { limit }`), from `yamt_range::Error` (`UnknownFile` → `UnknownRangeFile { file }`, everything else `Git` with its line), from `yamt_review::Error` (`WriteFailed { path, message }`, `UnknownFile` → `UnknownRangeFile`, `UnknownThread { thread }`, `UnknownMessage { message }`, `EmptyMessage`, `MessagePending { message }`; the start-only read refusals `Git` with their line) and from `yamt_agent::Error` (`Remove`/`Rename` → `RemoveFailed { folder, message }`, `Git` → `Git`), plus `MergeAborted`, `GitRunning`, `MergeFinished`, `WorkerStopped`, `SendRunning`, `AiOff`; every mapping's tests in `ipc_error/tests.rs`), `frontend_log.rs` (`LogEntry` → `tracing`, target `frontend`), `mock_window.rs` (tests only: a conflict or operation repository opened in a mock-runtime window, `invoke` a command by name, `invoke_on` from another thread, `ending()` calls `outcome::ending_when_git_is_done` — the close ending as `window.rs` computes it; used by the command tests in `commands.rs`, `merge/tests.rs` and `servers.rs`; `open_compare_window`: the compare window on a temp data folder, used by `compare.rs`; `range.rs` builds its own mock window over a `diverged_repo` and calls `invoke_on`). Merge window: `Mutex<Merge>` and `Mutex<Host>`; compare window: `Mutex<TabStore>`; range window: `Mutex<ThreadStore>`, the send guard `Mutex<()>` and `Mutex<AiState>` (its long holders: a prepare while git makes the checkout, a start while it reaps the earlier agent (up to about 3 s), a discard while it removes the folder, and the start's own-pair sweep; meanwhile the sync `send_to_agent`/`stop_agent` wait on the main thread). Never two held together, but for a send: it holds the send guard throughout and takes `threads` only between glab calls; a command locks one, calls one method and lets go; a worker never holds the merge's lock while git runs, nor the store's while it diffs, nor the AI's while it looks at the checkout or sweeps other pairs. `bin/export-bindings.rs` generates `frontend/src/ipc/bindings.ts` (`just bindings`). `tauri.conf.json` `bundle.resources` ships `LICENSE` and `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt` (`scripts/third-party-licenses.sh`) in every bundle. Depends on `session`, `settings`, `lsp-host`, `compare`, `range`, `review` and `agent` only, never on `gitio` or `merge-core` (arch-check).
